32
00:03:39,510 --> 00:03:53,030
As a recap of the vision we're building towards or if you're just catching up, Source is a new platform for modern teams of developers, designers, marketers, and more to build and optimize digital experiences with agents at the center.

33
00:03:53,806 --> 00:03:57,630
We talk to builders like you, marketing teams, and agencies all the time.

34
00:03:58,318 --> 00:04:02,564
And what we hear is that AI has made going from 0 to 1 incredibly fast.

35
00:04:03,022 --> 00:04:07,210
But most solutions lack the shared context, governance, and UI flexibility.

36
00:04:08,230 --> 00:04:11,950
Teams need to collaborate and drive impact at scale after that first build.

37
00:04:12,526 --> 00:04:15,110
And a prompt box isn't always the most effective way to build.

38
00:04:15,790 --> 00:04:20,930
To do your best work, you need best-in-class agents and best-in-class visual development tools.

39
00:04:21,510 --> 00:04:22,830
And that's what we're solving with Source.

40
00:04:24,814 --> 00:04:27,270
So let's talk a little bit more about how Source works.

41
00:04:27,890 --> 00:04:36,830
Source connects to your code base, CMS, and the other tools in your Martech stack so teams and agents can drive growth together in one shared, governed environment.

42
00:04:37,678 --> 00:04:42,590
For builders, that means building at the speed of AI with your code base as that source of truth.

43
00:04:43,214 --> 00:04:51,950
So agents can take on bigger, more complex changes without an abstraction layer holding them back, which really raises the ceiling of what you can create.

44
00:04:52,686 --> 00:04:56,250
So you can build with agents on a visual canvas or directly in code.

45
00:04:56,830 --> 00:04:58,436
And today we'll give you a preview of that.

46
00:04:59,214 --> 00:05:06,190
With Source, every marketer, designer, and developer gets a personalized workspace tailored to their job and the outcomes they own.

47
00:05:06,798 --> 00:05:09,650
So that's software that adapts to you and not the other way around.

48
00:05:09,678 --> 00:05:12,650
And this is where we're headed.

49
00:05:13,450 --> 00:05:19,390
Source is in a research preview today, an early version of the platform that's evolving with the people using and testing it.

50
00:05:19,822 --> 00:05:21,950
And some of whom I'm sure are in the audience today.

51
00:05:23,510 --> 00:05:33,810
So now before Matthew and Timothy jump into the live product, we wanna give everyone just a quick overview of what different key terms mean in Source so we're all speaking that same shared language.

52
00:05:34,766 --> 00:05:36,708
So starting on the left with Workspace.

53
00:05:37,358 --> 00:05:41,150
A workspace is the container for your people, your tools, and your work.

54
00:05:41,710 --> 00:05:43,230
And we're keeping it flexible on purpose.

55
00:05:43,822 --> 00:05:46,990
We don't force a data model on how you run your brand or your clients.

56
00:05:49,830 --> 00:05:52,290
And then inside a workspace, you have projects.

57
00:05:52,590 --> 00:05:56,010
And a project is really built around an outcome with a goal and a brief.

58
00:05:56,398 --> 00:05:57,430
So it's more than a folder.

59
00:05:58,230 --> 00:06:04,570
Projects can nest so a brand can have a project and its campaigns can then live inside of it.

60
00:06:04,686 --> 00:06:08,390
And your teammates and your agents can work from that same shared context.

61
00:06:09,470 --> 00:06:11,530
And then inside a project, we have sessions.

62
00:06:11,910 --> 00:06:17,210
And that's where you work with an agent and see which agent is running and what it's producing.

63
00:06:17,966 --> 00:06:24,050
And then this middle panel here on the right is the view, which Timothy and Matthew will be walking through in more detail today.

64
00:06:24,950 --> 00:06:34,830
And so views are a new powerful primitive of source and a dedicated customizable surface that allows you to shape your interface to the specific jobs you need to do and how you work.

65
00:06:35,370 --> 00:06:36,730
And this one here is the brand view.

66
00:06:37,326 --> 00:06:39,110
You can act on it as well as look at it.

67
00:06:40,398 --> 00:06:44,550
And then every view is made up of blocks, which you can think of as Lego pieces.

68
00:06:45,650 --> 00:06:47,990
So this colors pages is a stack of blocks.

69
00:06:48,630 --> 00:06:54,030
You can use ones we build, ones our partners and communities build, or build your own.

70
00:06:54,766 --> 00:06:58,890
And then we have specialized source agents, which can also help you assemble a view on the fly.

71
00:06:58,890 --> 00:07:03,210
And then, in fact, we just shipped our first iteration of our view builder agent yesterday.

72
00:07:04,270 --> 00:07:08,110
You can ask the view builder agent, what's happening with conversions on this page?

73
00:07:08,366 --> 00:07:11,170
And the agent builds that view that answers it.

74
00:07:11,438 --> 00:07:12,990
And if it's useful, you can keep it.

75
00:07:13,646 --> 00:07:15,470
So the view is where you apply your judgment.

76
00:07:16,170 --> 00:07:17,750
The agent is where work happens.

77
00:07:17,950 --> 00:07:22,890
And then governance, meaning roles, approvals, and audit logs is built into both.

78
00:07:24,494 --> 00:07:27,690
So now zooming out on kind of this technical architecture of source.

79
00:07:27,982 --> 00:07:29,530
we like to think of it as four layers.

80
00:07:30,290 --> 00:07:36,250
So at the top left is the source application, the primitives we just walked through, plus the agent in your inbox.

81
00:07:36,910 --> 00:07:41,970
At the top right are extensions, and this is how we, our partners, and you build into source.

82
00:07:42,478 --> 00:07:47,570
You can add your own views, blocks, tools, agents, and skills, first party or third party.

83
00:07:48,430 --> 00:07:51,670
Underneath that is shared context and intelligence, which is that brain.

84
00:07:52,206 --> 00:08:00,050
So connectors, analytics, evals, memory, and data sources are what let your work compound instead of starting from scratch every session.

85
00:08:01,006 --> 00:08:03,430
At the bottom, we have a platform and hosting.

86
00:08:03,950 --> 00:08:08,850
So runtime, deployment, MCP and CLI, governance, security and data residency.

87
00:08:09,806 --> 00:08:11,230
And that's what lets this run at scale.

88
00:08:11,950 --> 00:08:14,290
So putting that together, that's where we're after.

89
00:08:14,690 --> 00:08:19,490
Power at scale, workflows that compound and workspaces shaped around how you work.

